<title>FRANCE: Havas rises on talk of CLT stake move.</title>
<headline>Havas rises on talk of CLT stake move.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Havas rose sharply on Tuesday, boosted by speculation the CLT holding company controlled by Belgian businessman Albert Frere might take a big stake in the French media group.</p>
<p>&quot;Rumours of the rise of Albert Frere are sparking speculation on the stock,&quot; a trader said. Le Figaro reported Frere was set to sell his stakes in M6 and digital satellite television venture TPS and exchange CLT shares for a 22 percent holding in Havas. TPS denied the talk.</p>
<p>Havas was up 3.24 percent at 414 francs, on volume of 129,751 shares at 1044 GMT.</p>
</text>
